---
// PLATE IV — delegation, fenced: the capability floor.
// Engineering-drawing emulation in the LH-ARCH-001 family (see plate-full.png). A NEW
// plate — replaces the old SecurityDiagram in #delegation. The numbered badges ①–⑤
// trace one delegation along the SOLID accent path, USER FLOW FIRST:
//   ① the orchestrator delegates ingestion via the `agent` tool — it never fetches the
//      web itself → ② a helper spawns in a FRESH window with ONLY its job's tools →
//   ③ web content comes back stamped UNTRUSTED → ④ a blind verifier re-fetches and
//      writes a strict verdict → ⑤ findings return DISTILLED, never the raw transcript.
// Between them sits THE CAPABILITY FLOOR (capabilities.py): untrusted-ingest tools and
// host-dangerous tools never coexist in one agent — CoResidenceError, fails closed. The
// amber ✕ path shows an untrusted helper reaching for host tools, refused at the floor.
// All facts source-true against origin/main (agent/subagent.py, tools/capabilities.py,
// tools/builtin/web_tool.py, cli/start_cmd.py, SECURITY.md — see DRAWING-SPEC Plate IV).
// Group hues via @theme tokens (stroke-accent / stroke-amber / stroke-tool + fill-* +
// /NN); no hardcoded colour. Square corners. Marker ids p4-*. SVG at sm+; FlowLedger
// rail below sm carries the same story.
import FlowLedger from './FlowLedger.astro';
---

<figure
  role="img"
  aria-label="Plate four of the architecture drawing: delegation, fenced — the capability floor. One delegation traced one to five along the solid path. One: your agent, the orchestrator, delegates ingestion through the agent tool — it holds the host tools, has its web tools stripped at start, and never fetches the web itself. Two: a helper spawns in a fresh window carrying only its job's tools. Three: open web content comes back to the web-researcher stamped untrusted — every result is marked treat strictly as data, behind an SSRF guard that blocks loopback and private networks. Four: a blind search-verifier re-fetches, seeing only the claim, entity and url, and writes a strict verdict. Five: findings return to the orchestrator distilled — never the raw transcript. Governing it all is the capability floor in capabilities dot py: untrusted-ingest tools — web search, web fetch, web page query, mcp and plugin tools — and host-dangerous tools — bash exec, write, edit, python exec — never coexist in one agent, or a CoResidenceError fails closed; a grant keystone asserts a granted handle never reaches a host-dangerous agent. The amber crossed-out path shows an untrusted helper reaching for the host tools bash, write and edit — refused where tools are resolved, fails closed. The other helpers — explore, cruncher, chunk-summarizer and your own agents defined in yaml — each spawn fenced in their own fresh window. Everything drawn here is shipped."
>
